.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt COMPONENT 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm component
.Nd local authority replacement and global service model
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Programs managed by
.Xr serviced 8
use typed libraries instead of ambient discovery or raw IPC protocols.
There are two non-overlapping scopes.
.Ss Local descriptors
Local descriptors replace ambient filesystem, networking, or cryptographic authority removed
from a sandboxed process.
A bundle requests them with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
descriptors { network {} }
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr serviced 8
constructs every requested instance before exec, enlists its worker in the
consumer coalition, and injects a confined descriptor through a fixed
environment entry.
The Network library consumes that entry and exposes ordinary typed operations.
Mutable filesystem state is not requested here; a unit obtains its own dataset
at runtime from
.Xr tzfsd 8
by opening
.Dq system.Storage .
The application does not select a provider, protocol version, lifetime,
sharing mode, or options object.
Local descriptors are mandatory and are never looked up globally.
.Ss Global services
A provider declares one or more reverse-domain names:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
activation { ipc = ["org.example.control", "org.example.events"]; }
.Ed
.Pp
Any lookup of those names activates the one provider process.
Concurrent lookups of different names coalesce onto that same activation.
The provider uses
.Xr libservice 3
to expose one independent listener per name, and each incoming endpoint is
routed only to its addressed listener.
Registrations remain staged until the process has exposed its complete
.Va activation.ipc
set, entered capability mode, and completed
.Fn service_ready .
The entire endpoint set then becomes visible atomically.
Logging, notification, tracing, and third-party services use this model.
.Ss Failure model
Every accepted or connected session is a fresh direct channel.
Closing one session cannot consume another session's replies.
Peer exit revokes the opposite endpoint, so receive operations fail with
.Er ECONNRESET ,
send operations fail with
.Er EPIPE
or
.Er ECONNRESET ,
and pollers observe end-of-file.
If a provider exits during activation,
.Xr serviced 8
immediately fails all pending lookups instead of retaining them until a
startup timeout.
The libservice supervisor event descriptor reports permanent loss of
.Xr serviced 8 ;
listener descriptors also become readable and blocked accepts fail.
Already established peer channels remain independent of the naming
supervisor until a peer closes.
.Pp
Successful transport send means that the kernel accepted a message, not that
the provider committed the operation.
Typed protocols use nonzero channel reply tokens and typed replies to
acknowledge processing.
They may retry only operations whose protocol explicitly defines idempotency.
Exactly-once effects across provider crashes require provider-owned durable
deduplication and are not implied by
.Xr libservice 3 .
.Ss Security invariants
.Bl -bullet
.It
Typed application libraries own discovery and protocol validation.
.It
Global registration is authorized against the exact
.Va activation.ipc
list.
.It
Authenticated client identity comes from serviced, not client payload.
.It
Local authority descriptors are ready before exec, non-transferable, and
close-on-fork/exec constrained.
.It
Component workers join the consumer coalition and cannot outlive it.
.It
Security-relevant creation, denial, routing, and teardown paths provide
OpenBSM audit events and DTrace probes.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr serviced 5 ,
.Xr serviced 8
